# Secret. Only for the `restore-check` ops job: ${SF_SECRETS_DIR}/restore-test.env. A DISPOSABLE database that
# is never the staging database; its contents are overwritten. The script refuses a target with the same host,
# port and database name as DATABASE_URL, a target whose database name does not contain "restore", "test" or
# "scratch", and a target that resolves to the same server and database (identity check). URL shape: see
# migrate.env.example (query limited to sslmode, sslrootcert, connect_timeout; database name A-Za-z0-9_.-). The
# role needs to own/restore into the scratch database (force_migrator on a second database in the same server
# works). Percent-encode reserved characters in USER and PASSWORD.
RESTORE_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://REPLACE_USER:REPLACE_PASSWORD@REPLACE_HOST:5432/REPLACE_RESTORE_TEST_DB?sslmode=verify-full
# With sslmode=verify-full against a managed database, add &sslrootcert=<mounted CA file path> and mount that
# file read-only in the restore-check container (see migrate.env.example).
